{"archetypes":[{"name":"bootstrap-handoff","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's PREFLIGHT_TMPDIR→IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR log-migration step is underdefined against the repo's established handoff contract in SKILL.md around the --preflight-tmpdir bootstrap argument.","prompt_body":"Check whether the plan's proposed emergency-bypass log migration (copy $PREFLIGHT_TMPDIR/emergency-bypass.log into $IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/execution-issues.md \"as the first step after bootstrap\") is consistent with the existing bootstrap handoff contract in skills/implement/SKILL.md — specifically the --preflight-tmpdir argument passed to implement-bootstrap.sh at Step 0, which is the repo's established mechanism for threading Preflight-allocated artifacts into the IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR session. Verify whether the plan's migration is additive and compatible with that path, or whether it creates a parallel handoff channel that diverges from or conflicts with the established --preflight-tmpdir flow. Check whether the plan specifies which script or SKILL.md step performs the copy, and whether the named target path (execution-issues.md) and the append-tool-failure.sh pattern are consistent with how that file is created and consumed in the rest of the implement flow. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"flag-state-timing","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"persist-implement-run-flags.sh requires --implement-tmpdir (an existing directory) and is only called after Step 0, but EMERGENCY_REQUESTED is parsed and consumed during Preflight before that directory exists — the plan must thread flag state across that boundary without loss.","prompt_body":"Verify that the plan correctly handles the temporal gap between when --emergency is parsed (before Preflight, before IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR exists) and when persist-implement-run-flags.sh is called (after Step 0 bootstrap). Check the actual persist-implement-run-flags.sh contract: it requires --implement-tmpdir to be an existing directory and exits 2 otherwise; this means emergency_requested cannot be persisted until after bootstrap, yet the plan relies on it during Preflight. Confirm whether the plan has a defined mechanism for carrying the boolean flag value from the pre-Preflight parse through Step 0 into the persist call, or whether there is a state-loss window if bootstrap fails or diverges. Also check whether the plan's larch:metadata / larch:final-summary emission contract for EMERGENCY_REQUESTED is correctly grounded in the actual template structure in skills/implement/references/summary-comment-template.md — specifically whether that file has a metadata body schema that the plan's proposed Emergency: true|false line can slot into. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
